1
00:00:00,079 --> 00:00:02,990
Open Personnel to manage the
people in your department.

2
00:00:03,359 --> 00:00:08,640
The top actions include Add a Person,
Manage Invites and Manage Roles.

3
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:13,170
This walkthrough uses Add a Person to
create a fictional member directly.

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:16,459
Peter Mills will join a community
coordination group with a

5
00:00:16,459 --> 00:00:18,489
community response navigator role.

6
00:00:18,879 --> 00:00:23,370
Choosing the member’s group, operational
role and department access deliberately

7
00:00:23,370 --> 00:00:26,829
helps the roster reflect the work
that person is expected to do.

8
00:00:27,149 --> 00:00:30,540
Under Account Information,
enter a unique Username.

9
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:34,230
Enter a New Password and the
matching Confirm Password.

10
00:00:34,639 --> 00:00:38,779
The help here requires at least eight
characters, including a digit, an

11
00:00:38,819 --> 00:00:41,159
uppercase letter and a lowercase letter.

12
00:00:41,609 --> 00:00:44,269
The example keeps both
password fields masked.

13
00:00:44,650 --> 00:00:47,839
Review the actual requirements
on your form and use a separate

14
00:00:47,839 --> 00:00:49,079
credential for the member.

15
00:00:49,449 --> 00:00:53,919
The username identifies the account;
the profile details below identify

16
00:00:53,919 --> 00:00:55,859
the person on the department roster.

17
00:00:56,039 --> 00:01:00,000
In User Details, enter the
member’s I D Number, First Name,

18
00:01:00,199 --> 00:01:02,019
Last Name and Email Address.

19
00:01:02,420 --> 00:01:07,119
This fictional example uses Peter Mills
and a training-only identification number.

20
00:01:07,539 --> 00:01:10,840
The email help says Email
Addresses must be unique.

21
00:01:11,189 --> 00:01:15,530
Use the intended person’s correct details
in your own department so that the saved

22
00:01:15,530 --> 00:01:17,670
profile and roster are recognizable.

23
00:01:18,059 --> 00:01:22,030
These identity fields are separate from
the group and role selections that follow.

24
00:01:22,269 --> 00:01:26,160
Under Group Details, choose the
community coordination training group.

25
00:01:26,569 --> 00:01:29,629
Leave Is Group Admin
unchecked for this example.

26
00:01:30,169 --> 00:01:34,160
Under Roles, select the community
response navigator training role.

27
00:01:34,529 --> 00:01:37,170
The selected role appears
as a chip in the field.

28
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:42,479
Group membership, group administration and
a personnel role have separate controls.

29
00:01:42,799 --> 00:01:46,979
Assign the operational role the member
needs, then decide separately whether

30
00:01:46,979 --> 00:01:48,709
the person should administer the group.

31
00:01:49,119 --> 00:01:52,250
This exercise keeps that
administration checkbox clear.

32
00:01:52,470 --> 00:01:56,639
At the bottom, review Notify
User and Require Password Change.

33
00:01:56,959 --> 00:02:01,599
The first note says to uncheck Notify
User if you do not want Resgrid to notify

34
00:02:01,599 --> 00:02:03,379
the person of this account creation.

35
00:02:03,740 --> 00:02:06,170
It is unchecked for our
local training example.

36
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:09,869
Require Password Change is a
separate first-login choice,

37
00:02:09,910 --> 00:02:11,309
and remains unchecked here.

38
00:02:11,690 --> 00:02:14,590
Review those choices before
selecting Add Person.

39
00:02:15,059 --> 00:02:19,100
This lesson creates the account without
demonstrating a notification delivery

40
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:21,199
or a first-login password change.

41
00:02:21,309 --> 00:02:25,580
After Add Person, the saved Personnel
list can be filtered with Search.

42
00:02:25,939 --> 00:02:28,490
Search for Peter Mills and
check the matching row.

43
00:02:28,870 --> 00:02:32,490
It shows the community response
navigator role and a Normal state.

44
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:37,000
Staffing is Available and Status
is Standing By in this exercise.

45
00:02:37,359 --> 00:02:40,829
Read those separate columns instead
of assuming that a normal account

46
00:02:40,829 --> 00:02:44,230
state describes the person’s
current operational availability.

47
00:02:44,650 --> 00:02:47,820
Select Edit on this row to
review the saved profile.

48
00:02:48,029 --> 00:02:51,359
The reopened profile contains
the saved identity fields.

49
00:02:51,740 --> 00:02:53,199
Review Time Zone as well.

50
00:02:53,590 --> 00:02:57,840
In this example the initial selection
is Hawaii, which does not match the

51
00:02:57,840 --> 00:02:59,920
intended Chicago training context.

52
00:03:00,279 --> 00:03:02,890
Change it to Central Time, U S and Canada.

53
00:03:03,369 --> 00:03:06,940
Selecting the option prepares
a change; it is not saved yet.

54
00:03:07,329 --> 00:03:11,329
Continue to the bottom of the profile,
where the same Save action will store

55
00:03:11,329 --> 00:03:15,110
this time-zone change together with
the department settings we review next.

56
00:03:15,229 --> 00:03:19,629
Under Department Settings, keep
User Type set to Normal User rather

57
00:03:19,629 --> 00:03:21,350
than selecting Department Admin.

58
00:03:21,850 --> 00:03:26,580
Check Disable User and leave Hide
User clear, then select Save.

59
00:03:27,010 --> 00:03:31,390
Back in Personnel, Peter’s saved
State now reads Normal, Disabled.

60
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:36,390
The row still shows Available under
Staffing and Standing By under Status.

61
00:03:36,689 --> 00:03:40,950
That visible result is why account-state
controls and operational staffing or

62
00:03:40,950 --> 00:03:43,060
status should be reviewed separately.

63
00:03:43,419 --> 00:03:46,810
This recording verifies the
saved disabled state, without

64
00:03:46,810 --> 00:03:48,400
attempting a sign-in as Peter.

65
00:03:48,630 --> 00:03:50,569
Reopen Edit for the same member.

66
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:55,710
Keep Normal User selected, clear
Disable User, leave Hide User

67
00:03:55,750 --> 00:03:57,759
unchecked, and select Save.

68
00:03:58,179 --> 00:03:59,389
Search for Peter again.

69
00:03:59,889 --> 00:04:03,259
The saved State now reads Normal,
and the community response

70
00:04:03,259 --> 00:04:05,199
navigator role remains on the row.

71
00:04:05,619 --> 00:04:08,789
This readback confirms the
department-state change was stored.

72
00:04:09,340 --> 00:04:13,340
Use the same review-and-save approach
when an authorized administrator needs to

73
00:04:13,340 --> 00:04:17,619
change a member’s department access, and
check the result on the intended person.

74
00:04:17,819 --> 00:04:21,220
Reopening the profile also
confirms that Central Time, the

75
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:24,810
community coordination group and
the navigator role were retained.

76
00:04:25,370 --> 00:04:27,400
Is Group Admin remains clear.

77
00:04:28,020 --> 00:04:31,360
The same member setup applies
beyond fire and E M S.

78
00:04:31,760 --> 00:04:35,680
Community paramedicine and mental
health teams can organize coordinators;

79
00:04:36,010 --> 00:04:40,559
search-and-rescue and security departments
can organize field personnel; wildland

80
00:04:40,559 --> 00:04:44,440
contractors and industrial emergency
teams can organize their crews.

81
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:49,639
Use your own group and role names,
review the access settings, save, and

82
00:04:49,639 --> 00:04:51,750
verify the resulting member profile.
